unded by that clause's **unlock boundary** (that platform, within that premise's covered deployment environments, only). **2026-09-21 (B3b)**: a real power-loss injection matrix (main matrix 17 cells × 5 = 85 rounds all valid, U4 6 cells × 3 = 18 rounds, 0 true orphans; premise P′ = VirtualBox Win11B3 / NTFS on SATA-AHCI with `useHostIOCache=false` / record-level ~1 KiB / 2 s cut window / N=5) returned **C2 `proven`** with C1/C3/C2C3 `unresolved` (C3/C2C3 fail on **missing mechanism evidence** in their decision cells, which is the rig failing closed and **not** "not durable"); the candidate ordering is therefore **C2 first, with C3/C2C3 having established no claim**; **Windows `unproven` and the first-dispatch refusal are still unchanged** - protocol first, so the precondition for `ACCEPTED` remains the CONTRACTS durability-sentence revision under §7 "Publication-durability tiers and upgrade conditions" (its own slice, **B3c**, whose wording revision completed on 2026-09-21); rising to `ACCEPTED` still requires that platform's own complete evidence, an independent review, and a passing AT-23. See `docs/validation/t027-b3b-durability.md` (+ `_EN`) and the evidence pack `docs/validation/evidence/b3b-2026-09-21/` |
